    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0810" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Eddy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 131.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram of
                    June 11 last, I inclose copy of a note from the Japanese minister at this
                    capital, stating that, in view of information received by his Government that
                    the Japanese subjects at Caparison Djaore had been transferred to the interior,
                    his Government no longer deems it necessary to send a neutral vessel for the
                    withdrawal of the people in question.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d708-a1.xml" xpointer="d708-a1"/>
